<https://tolkiengateway.net/wiki/MECCG/TW-372> <https://tolkiengateway.net/wiki/MECCG/Property:quote> "“In a hole in the ground there lived a hobbit. Not a nasty, dirty, wet hole, filled with the ends of worms and an oozy smell, nor yet a dry, bare, sandy hole with nothing in it to sit down on or to eat: it was a hobbit-hole, and that means comfort.” —Hob"@en .
